{
	"_units": "Combined arms A1 (docs/combined_arms.md 2.4): armour per vehicle model, merged into the model's spec by VehicleSpecs.spec (docs/combined_arms.md 9.1: per-topic files keep parallel phases apart). A model with plates resolves rounds that have a data/shells.json or data/warheads.json row through ArmourModel; the rest (rifle rounds, charges, mines, fire support) keep VehicleDamage and the zone's armour class, as does a hit inside no plate. plates: boxes in the vehicle frame (front is -z), [x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1]; a hit takes the first plate in the list whose box holds it, whose normal faces the round and agrees with the voxel face it met (ArmourModel.plate_at). normal: the facing its figures apply along (published composite figures are line-of-sight values at their design facing, so they get that facing, not the voxel staircase's slope); \"any\" = head-on from every side (wheels, engine bays, small turrets). ke_mm / ce_mm: RHA-equivalent at the normal against kinetic / chemical-energy rounds; phys_mm: physical thickness (overmatch, HE punch-through, fuze sensitivity); material: rha, hhs, alu, composite, composite_du, glass, skirt, tyre (the x-ray and hit sounds); composite: obliquity capped at 2x instead of 4x; spaced_mm: an air gap behind the plate (a shaped charge loses min(15%, spaced_mm / 3000)). tiles: reactive armour and slat groups (light_era, heavy_era, tandem_era, slat), count tiles along the box's longest side, each used up when it fires; coverage = chance a round meets a tile, not a gap; package = fitted only with that package (any of a list); removed_by = taken off when one of those is fitted. belly: blast share under the hull and the seats (phase A2); spall_liner (phase A2); packages: what each upgrade does to the armour, its weight and who sells it (phase A8 buys and fits them; prices go in data/prices.json). Every number is Proposed, from public estimates (docs/combined_arms.md 2.4.2), rounded and tuned for balance.",
